# VXI-11 as ONC RPC calls and replies, with no sockets. `> PROGRAM PROC args...` is a call: PROGRAM is pmap (100000 v2), core
# (0x0607AF = 395183, v1) or abort (0x0607B0 = 395184, v1), PROC the procedure number, the args XDR words (decimal) and `s"text"` for opaque data (length,
# bytes, padding). The `<` line after it is the results of the accepted reply in the same notation (`ok` first), or `err STAT` for an
# RPC accept_stat other than success (1 PROG_UNAVAIL, 2 PROG_MISMATCH low high, 3 PROC_UNAVAIL, 4 GARBAGE_ARGS). `@ connect` is a new
# TCP connection (its links go). {version} is this crate's version. Escapes in text: \n, \", \\.

# The portmapper: where is the core channel (TCP; UDP has none)? 4881 is the port the test gives the service.
> pmap 3 395183 1 6 0
< ok 4881
> pmap 3 395183 1 17 0
< ok 0
> pmap 3 395184 1 6 0
< ok 4881
> pmap 3 12345 1 6 0
< ok 0
> pmap 1 395183 1 6 4881
< ok 0
> pmap 4
< ok 1 395183 1 6 4881 1 395184 1 6 4881 0
> pmap 0
< ok
> pmap 5
< err 3
> pmap 3 1
< err 4

# A link: create, write with END, read the response with its reason (END is 4), read the status byte (MAV is 16 while a response waits).
> core 10 7 0 0 s"inst0"
< ok 0 1 4881 1048576
> core 11 1 0 0 8 s"*IDN?\n"
< ok 0 6
> core 13 1 0 0 0
< ok 0 16
> core 12 1 100 0 0 0 0
< ok 0 4 s"ferrofire,rtu-1,0,{version}\n"
> core 13 1 0 0 0
< ok 0 0

# Reasons: the size (REQCNT 1), the termination character (CHR 2, flag 128), the end together with them.
> core 11 1 0 0 8 s"*IDN?"
< ok 0 5
> core 12 1 7 0 0 0 0
< ok 0 1 s"ferrofi"
> core 12 1 100 0 0 128 44
< ok 0 2 s"re,"
> core 12 1 100 0 0 128 10
< ok 0 6 s"rtu-1,0,{version}\n"

# -410: a write that starts a message while a response is unread drops the response. -420: a read with nothing to say, or while a
# message is half written.
> core 11 1 0 0 8 s"*IDN?"
< ok 0 5
> core 11 1 0 0 8 s"*OPC?"
< ok 0 5
> core 12 1 100 0 0 0 0
< ok 0 4 s"1\n"
> core 11 1 0 0 8 s"SYST:ERR?"
< ok 0 9
> core 12 1 100 0 0 0 0
< ok 0 4 s"-410,\"Query INTERRUPTED\"\n"
> core 12 1 100 0 0 0 0
< ok 15 0 s""
> core 11 1 0 0 0 s"*IDN?"
< ok 0 5
> core 12 1 100 0 0 0 0
< ok 15 0 s""
> core 11 1 0 0 8 s"SYST:ERR?"
< ok 0 9
> core 12 1 100 0 0 0 0
< ok 0 4 s"-420,\"Query UNTERMINATED\"\n"
> core 11 1 0 0 8 s"SYST:ERR?"
< ok 0 9
> core 12 1 100 0 0 0 0
< ok 0 4 s"-420,\"Query UNTERMINATED\"\n"

# Clear, trigger, remote and local are accepted; lock, interrupt channel and DOCMD are not supported; unlock has nothing to release.
> core 11 1 0 0 8 s"*IDN?"
< ok 0 5
> core 15 1 0 0 0
< ok 0
> core 12 1 100 0 0 0 0
< ok 15 0 s""
> core 14 1 0 0 0
< ok 0
> core 16 1 0 0 0
< ok 0
> core 17 1 0 0 0
< ok 0
> core 18 1 0 0 0
< ok 8
> core 19 1
< ok 12
> core 20 1 0 0 0
< ok 8
> core 22 1 0 0 0
< ok 8 0
> core 25 0 0 0 0 0
< ok 8
> abort 1 1
< ok 0

# Errors: an unknown link is 4 in the shape of each reply, another device name is 3, locking at create is 8.
> core 15 99 0 0 0
< ok 4
> core 12 99 100 0 0 0 0
< ok 4 0 0
> core 13 99 0 0 0
< ok 4 0
> core 10 7 0 0 s"gpib0,5"
< ok 3 0 4881 1048576
> core 10 7 1 0 s"inst0"
< ok 8 0 4881 1048576
> core 23 1
< ok 0
> core 23 1
< ok 4
> core 99
< err 3
> core 10 7
< err 4
> nobody 0
< err 1
